# .cluster-extra-sync — lists paths that are "gitignored but still needed on
# the node", one relative path per line (relative to the repo root). Lines
# starting with # are comments, blank lines are ignored. Paths must not be
# absolute and must not contain ..
#
# Purpose: these are typically local-only overrides, local-only credentials,
# etc. that genuinely shouldn't be in git, but are still needed when the code
# runs on the node. cluster_sync_up.sh does a separate rsync for each entry
# listed here (not a full-tree sync) after the git sync completes, and
# excludes these paths from the node's `git clean -fdx` cleanup of "files not
# in git" so they don't get wiped.
#
# Currently empty — CoSiR hasn't needed this mechanism yet (dataset caches go
# through DATA_LOCAL_BASE/DATA_REMOTE_BASE, results go through RESULTS_REMOTE,
# both already independent sync paths, no need to duplicate them here). If a
# future need comes up — e.g. some dataset's _cluster.yaml depends on a
# local-only credential file, or a hydra override that's only used on the node
# and shouldn't be committed — just add a relative path, e.g.:
#   configs/local/node_secrets.yaml
